%I A402499 #27 Nov 22 2026 16:47:10
%S A402499 3,5,13,61,421,4621,60061,1021021,19399381,446185741,12939386461,
%T A402499 401120980261,14841476269621,608500527054421,26165522663340061,
%U A402499 1229779565176982821,65178316954380089461,3845520700308425278141,234576762718813941966541,15716643102160534111758181
%N A402499 a(n) = 2*prime(n)# + 1, where prime(n)# = A002110(n).
%C A402499 For n >= 1, a(n) == 5 (mod 8) is a quadratic residue modulo every prime 3 <= p <= prime(n).
%C A402499 Sequence forms a compatible system modulo {4*prime(n)#}: a(n) mod 4*prime(m)# = a(m) for n >= m >= 1.
%C A402499 Let N = A102476(n+1) be the least modulus with 2^(n+1) square roots of 1. For n >= 1, the minimal element of the coset of (Z/NZ)*^2 in (Z/NZ)* containing a(n), or the least m coprime to N such that a(n)/m is a square modulo N, is m = A401305(n-1). Here (Z/NZ)* is the multiplicative group of integers modulo N and (Z/NZ)*^2 is the subgroup of squares.
%C A402499 For any fundamental discriminant D of a quadratic field dividing N (n >= 1), kronecker(D,a(n)) = -1 if and only if 8 divides D.
%H A402499 Jianing Song, <a href="/A402499/b402499.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..350</a>
%t A402499 2*FoldList[Times, 1, Prime[Range[20]]] + 1 (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 22 2026 *)
%o A402499 (PARI) my(P=2); forprime(p=2, 100, print1(P+1, ", "); P*=p)
%o A402499 (PARi) a(n) = 2*vecprod(primes(n)) + 1; \\ _Michel Marcus_, Nov 22 2026
%Y A402499 Cf. A002110.
%Y A402499 Let N = 4*p# (A102476).
%Y A402499 Sequences related to residues modulo N: this sequence (N/2+1), A228698 (N-1), A402500 (N/3+1 or 2*N/3+1, 2 mod 3), A006862 (N/4+1), A402501 (3*N/4+1), A402502 (N/4+1 or 3*N/4+1, 7 mod 8), A402503 (N/4+1 or 3*N/4+1, 3 mod 8), A402504 (N+1), A282704 (N/2-1), A402505 (N/3-1 or 2*N/3-1, 1 mod 3), A057588 (N/4-1), A402506 (3*N/4-1).
%Y A402499 Primes p such that ... is prime: A119834 (N/2+1), A402427 (N-1), A402431 (N/3+1 or 2*N/3+1, 2 mod 3), A005234 (N/4+1), A402456 (3*N/4+1), A402426 (N+1), A402432 (N/3-1 or 2*N/3-1, 1 mod 3), A006794 (N/4-1), A402457 (3*N/4-1).
%Y A402499 Representatives of cosets of (Z/NZ)*^2 containing ... in (Z/NZ)*: A401305 (N/2+1), A045535 (N-1), A401356 (N/3+1 or 2*N/3+1, 2 mod 3), A402507 (N/4+1 or 3*N/4+1, 7 mod 8), A402547 (N/4+1 or 3*N/4+1, 3 mod 8).
